    opening: "A chargeback reverses a payment after a customer disputes a card transaction. A merchant can also lose dispute fees, fulfillment spending and sometimes the item itself. To price the risk, calculate the loss on each resolved dispute and spread the expected loss across all orders from the same period. Keep returns and disputes in separate records so the same order is not counted twice.",
